.env
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# generated native folders
/ios
/android

# NOTE: google-services.json is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It is the Firebase Cloud Messaging config for Android push. EAS uploads the
# project to its build servers with `git archive`, which excludes ignored
# files — so ignoring this one would mean it never reaches the build and push
# would silently never work, which is exactly how the Firebase env vars were
# lost earlier in this project's history.
#
# It contains public project identifiers (project id, sender id, and an
# Android API key restricted to this app's package + signing certificate) —
# the same class of value as the VITE_FIREBASE_* config already shipped in
# the web bundle. It is not a secret. The FCM *service account key*, which
# is a real secret, is uploaded to Expo and never stored here.
